\section{Results and Discussion}\label{s4}
The use of robust integration techniques to analyze analytical soliton solutions is novel and different from previous results obtained using different methods. We obtained proofs of analytical soliton wave solutions such as hyperbolic functions, weakly acting functions, value functions and the problem of triangular function solutions of the ill possed Boussinesq equation. Therefore, the solutions we obtained were converted back to the ill possed Boussinesq equation and analyzed using mathematical symbols in the Mathematica software. In order to explain the physical result of these solutions with 3D, and 2D Density graphs using the appropriate values of unknown coefficients and regular measurements, the observations are given as follows: Figures 1 and 2 shows the periodic waves of solution of (3.5),(3.6), Figures 5, 9, 12, 15 shows Dark solitons of the solution of (3.8), (3.13), (3.17), (3.20). Figure 8 shows the kink shaped soliton of solution of (3.12). Figure 11 shows the anti Kink shaped soliton of solution of (3.16). Figure 10 shows a dispersion-less soliton of solution of (3.14). The dynamical behavior of the analytical soliton solutions is presented by setting
the suitable values of unknown coefficients and free parameter constants.
\section{Conclusion}\label{s5}
\noindent This paper proposes a Unified Approach Method to solve the ill possed Boussinesq equation and produces different new solutions. Also, the solutions we obtained from the Unified approach method are not yet been published. Also, these new solutions might gives us the existing results and help to make the physical properties of the equations with much more clearity. The solutions are obtained by using Maple Software. This method is very general as well as simple and easy for finding the exact solutions of NLPDE's, which shows the efficiency, productivity and suitability of this method for handling many other non linear partial differential equations (NPDE's)
